{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Low-e",
  "Notes": "Low-emissivity glazing: two silver layers, visible transmission with IR reflection\n\nCaveats:\n- Manufacturability is scored with MINT/MAXT (minimum and maximum layer thickness) at a low weight. A sensitivity term (SENS) would score robustness to thickness errors directly, but it needs second derivatives of the merit function and is not offered; MINT/MAXT keep layers depositable and have exact derivatives.\n- The real specification is luminous transmittance and emissivity, band integrals against an illuminant and a blackbody. This samples the two bands instead: the same intent, not the same number.\n- Silver\u0027s index is a constant here, though it is strongly dispersive across 400-2400 nm. For a realistic design, replace it with the database Ag (Edit \u003E Materials).",
